# HoverIt

Android app (Kotlin + Jetpack Compose, glassmorphism) that flies the ESP32 SuperMini drone over Wi-Fi, plus the drone-side receiver `HoverItRx.h`.

## Run the app
1. Android Studio (Ladybug or newer) > Open > the `HoverIt` folder. Let Gradle sync (AGP 8.7.3, Kotlin 2.0.21, Compose BOM 2024.12.01, Gradle 8.11.1 wrapper).
2. Plug in the phone with USB debugging on and press Run. minSdk 26 (Android 8), landscape only.

## Set up the drone
1. Copy `HoverItRx.h` next to your flight controller sketch.
2. Put your phone hotspot name and password in `HOTSPOT_SSID` / `HOTSPOT_PASS`.
   No hotspot? `#define HOVERIT_SOFTAP 1` before the include and join the phone to the "HoverIt" network (password `hoverit123`).
3. Follow the example at the bottom of the header, or use `drone/FlightController.ino` (full flight controller with PID tuning from the app).
4. Turn on the hotspot, power the drone, open the app, tap Connect. It turns green when telemetry arrives.

## Screens
- Startup: animated HoverIt logo, then the stick screen.
- Sticks: left = throttle (Y, holds) + yaw (X, springs back); right = pitch/roll (both spring back). The left pad shows the flight mode and what the drone is doing, the right pad its height. Land locks the throttle stick, Autonomous locks both.
- Options, left: the four flight modes (Stabilize, Loiter, Land, Autonomous, see `drone/FlightController/FlightModes.h`). Tapping one always opens the stick screen in that mode. Land/Autonomous are never remembered between app starts.
- Options, right: Tuning Mode, Baro Training (on = training flight when armed on the ground, off = kill), Theme (Red = coral/magenta, Blue = sky/royal blue with the background recoloured blue).
- Tuning: the top-right button enables / disables the sliders (off by default; off = locked, and switching off while disarmed saves on the drone). Pick a PID loop at the top left (ROLL+PITCH rate, YAW RATE, VERT VEL = vertical velocity), then the KP, KI, KD, FF sliders (0-255). Picking a loop loads the drone's values into the sliders, moving one changes it live.
- Centre column on every screen: Connect (green connected / red not), Arm/Disarm (green disarmed / red armed), Options (fills with water to battery/255; the water stays level as you tilt the phone, ui/Tilt.kt).

## Link (UDP)
| Direction | Port | Rate | Bytes |
|---|---|---|---|
| phone -> drone | 4210 | 50 Hz | `'H' seq thr yaw pitch roll kp ki kd ff loop flags ver xor` (14) |
| drone -> phone | 4211 | 10 Hz | `'D' seq battery flags loop kp ki kd ff height status xor` (12) |

`flags` (phone): bit0 armed, bit1 baro training, bit2 tuning sliders enabled, bits 4-5 flight mode (0 Stabilize, 1 Loiter, 2 Land, 3 Autonomous). `flags` (drone): bit0 armed, bit1 training flight running, bits 4-5 mode being flown. `height` = cm / 2, `status` = `FlightStatus` (FlightModeCommon.h; FLIGHT_STATUS in DroneLink.kt).
Protocol version 3: an older app or drone sketch will not talk to this one, so update both.
`loop`: 0 roll + pitch rate, 1 yaw rate, 2 vertical velocity (climb rate). The angle and height loops are fixed constants on the drone (AttitudePID.h, HeightPID.h).
The drone broadcasts telemetry until the phone answers, so no IP needs typing.

## Safety
- Drone failsafe: no packet for 500 ms -> disarmed, sticks centred, throttle 0.
- App: shows disconnected after 1 s without telemetry and disarms itself.
- Arming needs throttle at the bottom (app and drone both check); the drone needs a fresh 0 -> 1 arm press.
